From: Alejandro Arrufat <15357691+AlexArrufat@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gsupplicant: enable SAE hash-to-element with legacy compatibility

The default sae_pwe=0 only enables hunting-and-pecking. Enable both
SAE derivation methods so access points advertising hash-to-element
can negotiate it without excluding older networks.

Set the per-interface global SaePwe property to "2" before connection
setup. This allows hash-to-element where advertised while retaining
hunting-and-pecking for older networks. It does not force WPA3 on
WPA2-only APs or change the list of permitted key-management methods.
NetworkManager uses the same global supplicant setting.

This complements the SAE D-Bus capability reporting fix in
wpa_supplicant 2.12. Tested with ConnMan 2.0:
WPA3-SAE, H2E, PMF, DHCP, and interface-bound traffic.

Upstream: Not submitted
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Arrufat <15357691+AlexArrufat@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/gsupplicant/supplicant.c
+++ b/gsupplicant/supplicant.c
@@ -2538,11 +2538,11 @@
 	return interface;
 }
 
-static void set_pmf(DBusMessageIter *iter, void *user_data)
-{
-	const char *pmf = user_data;
-
-	dbus_message_iter_append_basic(iter, DBUS_TYPE_STRING, &pmf);
+static void set_global_string(DBusMessageIter *iter, void *user_data)
+{
+	const char *value = user_data;
+
+	dbus_message_iter_append_basic(iter, DBUS_TYPE_STRING, &value);
 }
 
 static void interface_added(DBusMessageIter *iter, void *user_data)
@@ -2575,7 +2575,14 @@
 	 */
 	supplicant_dbus_property_set(path, SUPPLICANT_INTERFACE ".Interface",
 				"Pmf", DBUS_TYPE_STRING_AS_STRING,
-				set_pmf, NULL, "1", NULL);
+				set_global_string, NULL, "1", NULL);
+
+	/* Prefer SAE hash-to-element where advertised by the AP, while
+	 * retaining hunting-and-pecking compatibility for older networks.
+	 */
+	supplicant_dbus_property_set(path, SUPPLICANT_INTERFACE ".Interface",
+				"SaePwe", DBUS_TYPE_STRING_AS_STRING,
+				set_global_string, NULL, "2", NULL);
 
 	if (!properties_appended) {
 		supplicant_dbus_property_get_all(path,
